# Ruling §21 + J24 job list for jobq2.py. DO NOT START until the coordinator says so; run it from a clean
# checkout of the POST-O4 tag (this file is the only place the bound family and the J24 bounds are queued,
# so no bound output -- R21_* or J24_bound_* -- is produced on pre-O4 code; jobs/j24.jsonl is retired).
#   cd <post-O4 tree> && nohup python3 -I jobq2.py jobs/r21.jsonl > logs_jobq2_r21.txt 2>&1 &
# Every job declares outputs (jobq2 refuses jobs without them, §21.1). The runner is hard-killed at 2 h
# wall, so every job is <= ~100 min (p6 timings at 15 min on one core: bound main 11 min/city, ruled 7,
# sb 15, tariff 12, csw ~40, MPC in rules 1/6/24 h ~15 min/city, shield latch 3 s, shield PPO 11 s/model,
# t1_sens 3 s/city, clv_refine ~5 min/city, bound_at < 5 min).
# §21.4 producers (independent of O4): R21_D1_*, R21_J6ii_* (R1 = each city's fitted guard on,
#   T26v3_guard_fit p6: 23.6 / 23.62 / 23.66; R2 = 22.4), R21_T1_sens.
# Bound family on the O4 terminal (§21.3; includes the reruns of the killed Taif J8_9 / J10 jobs):
#   R21_J8_9_*, R21_J10_*, R21_J8_clv_*, R21_J15_sbbound_*, R21_J19_tariff_bound, R21_T5_bound, R21_bound_at.
# J24 (F23, merged from jobs/j24.jsonl; V-code-48):
#   * the J24 bounds run here, on the O4 code, like every other bound;
#   * J24_mpc_dt5_riyadh is the one job that would exceed ~100 min at 1601 nodes (MPC cost ~ 1/dt^2:
#     ~70 min, up to ~100 min with the §16 back-off knob). DISCLOSED COST REDUCTION: it runs at 801 nodes
#     (half the cost, ~35-50 min). At 15 min, 801 -> 1601 moved MPC-24 by 0.25-0.60 pt (§15), below the
#     3-pt resolution rule; the 5-min row of tab:s-timestep is footnoted "801-node grid". J24_bound_dt5
#     (~32 min) and every other J24 job are unchanged and well under the limit.
#   * J24_table also waits for R21_J8_9_bound_riyadh. CAUTION: its --headline dirs (p9:p6) hold the PRE-O4
#     15-min B* (T17v3_riyadh); before the table is cited, point --headline at the post-O4 results for T17v3.
